WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.247 --> 00:00:07.020
"The Best Diet for COVID and Long-COVID"

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.495
What’s the role of nutrition for both
preventing and beating COVID-19?

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.400
Nutrition-related myths
on protection and treatment

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.680
have been widely
prevalent in this pandemic,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.980
and while there is no diet
that completely prevents infection

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.340
there are certainly dietary steps
we can take to minimize risk.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.880
Those with healthier diets
in general, seem to suffer

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.660
less serious courses, but this appears
to be an indirect benefit

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.660
of lower rates of obesity
and pre-existing medical conditions.

00:00:33.945 --> 00:00:37.980
I mean, that’s great, but is there any diet
that may have direct effects

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.960
on the course of disease
or susceptibility

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.340
to infection in the first place?

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.100
Well, plant-based diets
have been shown to decrease

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:47.040
the risk of suffering from other
respiratory infections—in fact,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.380
plant-based seminaries
during the pandemic of 1918

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.300
appeared to have been
relatively spared.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.760
Why might a plant-based diet help?

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.840
Vegetable nitrates concentrated
in dark green leafy vegetables

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.400
can be used to make nitric oxide,

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.400
which is part of our lungs’ first line
of defense against infection.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.640
There are also polyphenol
phytonutrients in plants

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.620
that may directly inhibit
viral infection.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.800
Then there are beneficial
effects on our microbiome,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.440
which plays a key role in our
system-wide immune function.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.760
Fiber-containing foods facilitate
more of a symbiotic relationship

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.340
with our gut bugs, whereas
processed junk and animal foods

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.320
can have the opposite,
dysbiotic effect.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.860
Fiber, concentrated
in whole plant foods,

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.440
is the single most anti-inflammatory
food component,

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.140
whereas saturated fat, concentrated
in meat, dairy, and junk,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.540
is the most pro-inflammatory
food component.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.754
And so, no surprise
those consuming

00:01:35.754 --> 00:01:37.159
more pro-inflammatory diets

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.180
were at greater risk
of suffering a severe course,

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.340
and of getting COVID-19
in the first place,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.440
up to nearly
twelve times the odds,

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.390
even after taking
into account body weight,

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:46.920
diabetes, and blood pressure.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.760
But this study only covered
60 COVID patients.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.460
How about 11,000 COVID patients?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.800
Diet-associated
inﬂammation increased

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.752
the risk of getting
COVID-19 infection,

00:01:57.752 --> 00:02:01.020
suffering a severe course
and dying from the disease.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.900
Might this help explain
why the COVID death rates

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.760
were a hundred times
lower in Africa?

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.620
Can a plant-based diet
help mitigate

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.160
COVID-19? Let’s find out.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.000
In this study of COVID-19 illness
severity in the elderly

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.900
in relation to vegetarian versus
non-vegetarian diets, statistically,

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.260
the nonvegetarians had up to
like 20 times the odds

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.660
of suffering a critically
severe course of COVID,

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.900
but that was based
on only nine vegetarians.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:30.900
Now here, a study of thousands
of front-line healthcare workers

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.720
across six countries found that
those eating plant-based diets

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.720
had 73 percent lower odds
of suffering a moderate

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.352
or severe course
of COVID-19,

00:02:38.352 --> 00:02:40.286
and even combined
with pescatarians

00:02:40.402 --> 00:02:44.700
(who eat fish but no other meat)
still had significantly lower odds.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.782
The biggest spread was between
those eating plant-based

00:02:47.782 --> 00:02:49.140
versus low-carb.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:50.880
Compared to plant-based
healthcare workers,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.886
those eating low carb,
high-protein diets had nearly

00:02:52.886 --> 00:02:56.594
four times greater odds of suffering
a serious infection.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.280
This may not seem
surprising given that many

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.700
of the underlying risk factors
for COVID-19 mortality—obesity,

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.860
heart disease, high blood pressure,
and type 2 diabetes—

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.800
can be controlled or even
reversed with a healthy enough

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.000
plant-based diet and lifestyle.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.020
But the apparent plant-based
protection went above and beyond.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.640
The greatly reduced risk was
independent of all those conditions.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.220
The researchers suggest
that a "healthy diet

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.400
rich in nutrient-dense foods
may be considered for protection

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.800
against severe COVID-19."

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.200
The one food group most associated

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.680
with lower symptom severity
in one outpatient study was legumes,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.980
followed by grains, the top sources
of dietary fiber.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.920
The investigators suggest
that the anti-inflammatory effects

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.920
of the short-chain fatty acids
released by our fiber-feeding

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.684
good gut bugs may explain
the connection.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.520
The healthcare worker study
enrolled a few thousand people,

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.620
but Harvard researchers
collected data

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.520
from nearly 600,000 participants
using a plant-based diet

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.940
scoring system where you get
points for eating healthy plant foods,

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.300
but points deducted for meat,
eggs, junk, and dairy.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.100
And indeed those scoring
higher not only had

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.280
a significantly lower risk of suffering
a severe course of COVID-19,

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.560
but also a significantly lower risk

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.180
of getting infected
in the first place.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.780
And again, this was after taking
comorbidities into account,

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.440
alongside nondietary risk factors
such as exercise and smoking.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.220
The bottom line: "the best
available evidence suggests

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.340
that plant-based diets are beneﬁcial
in directly reducing the risk

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.860
of severe COVID-19 symptoms
and the risk of infection,"

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.860
even independent of other
health-related factors.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:32.280
A more Mediterranean-style
diet may reduce the risk

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.540
of infection by 22 percent,

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.520
while an even more
plant-based diet

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.724
may cut infection risk in half.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.200
For dealing with long COVID, a plant-
based diet has been suggested

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.960
based on the abundance of data
showing positive associations

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.300
of plant-based diets
with improved immune function,

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.120
neurotransmitter balance, pain
and inﬂammation reduction,

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.560
improved sleep, and mental health.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.220
So, in terms of lifestyle adjustments
in long-COVID management,

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:58.860
"large-scale promotion
of plant-based eating"

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.920
may have the potential to improve
physical and mental impacts,

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.560
but this has yet
to be put to the test.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:08.220
There was a study that suggested
that those who eat more vegetables

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.840
are less likely to end up depressed,

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.120
and those who eat more nuts,
beans, and whole grains

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.880
may end up less depressed, anxious,
and stressed after COVID-19,

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.000
whereas stress levels were
correlated with higher meat intake.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.360
But the only interventional
studies are like this,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:25.140
showing a detrimental impact
on high-fat high-sugar diets,

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.120
but that’s in Syrian hamsters,

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.420
though there are definitely
some unhappy hamster lungs

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:31.979
on the crappy diet.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.054
All in all, adopting
a healthy plant-based diet

00:05:35.054 --> 00:05:38.340
may be a powerful tool to decrease
the risk of severe COVID-19

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.280
and should be promoted as
a public health safety measure.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.080
And what are the side-effects?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:45.660
A delay in aging
and decreased disease.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.240
Maybe this is the booster we need.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.960
After all, if real effort
had gone into encouraging

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.180
and incentivizing healthier diets
and lifestyles,

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:57.060
we would not only have saved
many more lives from COVID-19,

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:59.820
but we would also reduce
future mortality

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:03.249
from all major causes of death.

